SK-0.5 — merge-based CSG booleans and post-fill level-set pruning.

Two changes to PicoGKVdbVoxels.h, both value-neutral (proved against this repo's
byte-locked fixture corpus: identical raw levelSetVolume, identical mesh-roundtrip
volume, identical STL bytes, identical triangle counts on all five subjects).

U-SK05-a  BoolAdd/BoolSubtract/BoolIntersect deep-copied the WHOLE operand grid
          before calling csgUnion/csgDifference/csgIntersection, because those
          steal from their second argument. openvdb's merge operators
          (tools/Merge.h) accept a DeepCopy tag that copies only the nodes
          actually grafted and tracks consumption in a lightweight mask tree —
          the same operator, the same top-down DynamicNodeManager traversal and
          the same terminating pruneLevelSet that Composite.h's csg* wrappers
          run. One full-grid materialization per boolean disappears. Measured at
          0.1 mm on a 78 MB operand: heap high-water 442.5 MB -> 368.8 MB.

U-SK05-b  The fills that walk a dense accessor over a bounding box
          (RenderImplicit, RenderLattice, ProjectZSliceUp/Dn) allocate a leaf for
          every 8^3 block they touch, including blocks that end up uniformly
          +background or -background. The csg paths already end in pruneLevelSet;
          these did not, so every downstream op iterated the slack. Measured
          reduction: RenderImplicit -68.1%, ProjectZSlice -36.1%,
          RenderLattice -5.5% of tree memory.

Upstream status: both are candidates to report to LEAP 71 (leap71/PicoGKRuntime).
Neither changes the public API or any produced value.

